Save the dashboard with name "System Monitoring"
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Grafana Service Won't Start
# Check service logs
sudo journalctl -u grafana-server -n 50

# Check configuration syntax
sudo grafana-server -config /etc/grafana/grafana.ini -test

# Verify file permissions
ls -la /etc/grafana/
sudo chown -R grafana:grafana /etc/grafana/
Issue 2: Cannot Access Web Interface
# Check if service is listening
sudo netstat -tlnp | grep 3000

# Check firewall settings
sudo ufw status
sudo ufw allow 3000

# Verify configuration
grep -n "http_port" /etc/grafana/grafana.ini
Issue 3: Prometheus Connection Failed
# Test Prometheus connectivity
curl -I http://localhost:9090

# Check Prometheus logs
sudo journalctl -u prometheus -n 20

# Verify configuration
sudo promtool check config /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml
Issue 4: No Metrics Available
# Check Node Exporter
curl http://localhost:9100/metrics | head -20

# Verify Prometheus targets
curl http://localhost:9090/api/v1/targets | jq '.'

# Check scrape configuration
cat /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml
Verification Steps
Verify Grafana Installation
# Check Grafana version
grafana-server --version

# Verify service status
sudo systemctl is-active grafana-server
sudo systemctl is-enabled grafana-server

# Check listening ports
sudo ss -tlnp | grep 3000
Verify Prometheus Setup
# Check Prometheus status
sudo systemctl is-active prometheus
curl -s http://localhost:9090/-/healthy

# Verify Node Exporter
sudo systemctl is-active node_exporter
curl -s http://localhost:9100/metrics | wc -l
Verify Data Source Integration
Access Grafana at http://localhost:3000
Navigate to Configuration > Data Sources
Verify Prometheus shows as Connected
Test queries in Explore section
Confirm dashboard displays metrics correctly
